# Features: each detection in a folder of its own (Features/<Name>/), which
# registers itself into the registries of Core/ and UI/ above, so it loads
# after them: Kind, Data (its static tables), Text, Mark, Slip or Card,
# then Capture. Its Dev.lua
# goes in the block at the foot (.claude/registry-refactor.md). Chat is
# first: its Dev.lua writes Tester's first session's whispers before the
# campfire's row.
Features/Chat/Kind.lua
Features/Chat/Capture.lua
Features/Campfire/Kind.lua
Features/Campfire/Text.lua
Features/Campfire/Mark.lua
Features/Campfire/Slip.lua
Features/Campfire/Capture.lua
Features/ProfessionCaps/Kind.lua
Features/ProfessionCaps/Text.lua
Features/ProfessionCaps/Mark.lua
Features/ProfessionCaps/Capture.lua
Features/QuestFinales/Kind.lua
Features/QuestFinales/Data.lua
Features/QuestFinales/Text.lua
Features/QuestFinales/Mark.lua
Features/QuestFinales/Capture.lua

Capture/Trade.lua
Capture/Menus.lua
Capture/Group.lua
Capture/Together.lua
Capture/Deaths.lua
Capture/PvP.lua
Capture/Nearby.lua
Capture/Sightings.lua
Capture/Journey.lua
Capture/Combat.lua
Capture/Witnesses.lua

#@do-not-package@
# Development tooling: diagnostics, /sd art, /sd journey and /sd testdata. They
# register their own /sd commands. The packager strips this block, so a
# release never loads them (.pkgmeta leaves the folder out as well, and
# every Features/*/Dev.lua). A feature's Dev.lua adds its test data to
# /sd testdata (TestData.Register), so it comes after Dev/TestData.lua.
Dev/Art.lua
Dev/Diagnostics.lua
Dev/SightingsDebug.lua
Dev/JourneyDebug.lua
Dev/TestData.lua
Features/Chat/Dev.lua
Features/Campfire/Dev.lua
Features/ProfessionCaps/Dev.lua
Features/QuestFinales/Dev.lua
#@end-do-not-package@
